{
  "transcriptVersion": 1,
  "id": "redirect-web-happy",
  "description": "A web app signs a person in through authorize and token (I-08, WIRE-CONTRACT-V4 §12.4, §12.5). The browser navigates to authorize (response_type, client_id, redirect_uri, state, an S256 challenge, scope) and is sent to the card; the person presses Continue, which answers the redirect carrying code, state and the issuer (RFC 9207); the SDK checks state and iss and redeems the code at token with a form body and its PKCE verifier. The answer is the browser device token (access_token), the granted scope, the device, a null licence on a licence-less device and the pairwise subject: never a token in a URL. The same code again is invalid_grant.",
